{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>He says:</b> this is the curse — the imprecation." "And the sense of <b>that goes out over the face of all the earth</b> — for it includes the Jews who were in Jerusalem and those who remained in Babylonia and in the land of Persia." "And the sense of <b>from this side like that</b> — for it was written in the scroll: on this side, the thief is cleared; on the other side, the one who swears is cleared — or from this side and from that side, for the thief and the one who swears are cleared, and this is correct." "And the sense of <b>cleared</b> — that each one, the one who exacts and the one who swears, will think that HaShem has cleared him."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "The phrase מזה כמוה renders the verse's מזה כמוה; the logic is compressed and the translation preserves the compression without expansion.", 3 "הגובה literally 'the one who lifts/takes'; context (swearing falsely) suggests the creditor or claimant, but the term is ambiguous and rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:02.844718759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}